class.description:
A selection is a list of point indices, not a copy of the geometry. Filtering and splitting build new selections without touching attribute values, so narrowing a hundred thousand points down to the few hundred you want costs almost nothing; only [method get_points] assembles data, and only for the points the selection holds.

Selections chain, which is how one HDA output feeds several handlers:
[codeblock]
var scattered = output.filter_by("hego_spawn", 1)
var by_path = scattered.split_by("hego_node_path")
for node_path in by_path:
    var points = by_path[node_path].get_points(["N", "up", "pscale"])
[/codeblock]

Obtained from [method HEGoGeoOutput.select_all], [method HEGoGeoOutput.filter_by] or [method HEGoGeoOutput.split_by].
